00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:56.513
North Vancouver Mayor Linda Buchanan is the new chair of the Metro Vancouver Regional District,

00:01:56.513 --> 00:02:02.173
Elected Friday, November 27, for a one-year term, with Coquitlam Mayor Craig Hodge as

00:02:02.173 --> 00:02:05.433
vice chair at the inaugural meeting after last month's civic election.

00:02:05.913 --> 00:02:11.153
She succeeds Burnaby Mayor Mike Hurley, chair since June 2024, who did not seek the

00:02:11.153 --> 00:02:14.913
role again, after 14 of 21 municipalities changed mayors.

00:02:15.453 --> 00:02:19.153
Yesterday Doug McCallum was running for this chair in order to eliminate the job.

00:02:19.793 --> 00:02:24.473
Buchanan in a statement praised employees and the services they deliver, then said public

00:02:24.473 --> 00:02:28.313
confidence and trust have been eroded. The financial path is not sustainable,

00:02:28.673 --> 00:02:33.473
and the organization as built is no longer fit for purpose. She wants fundamental reform,

00:02:33.873 --> 00:02:38.033
not a small adjustment, and her first step is a meeting with Hodge and Cathy Aunsted,

00:02:38.413 --> 00:02:42.893
the Minister of Local Government, Housing, Sport and Culture, to learn what the conservative

00:02:42.893 --> 00:02:47.873
government expects. That meeting is supposed to set a 100-day plan on what the district does,

00:02:48.253 --> 00:02:53.373
how it pays, and how it answers to the public. One piece asks which services stay and how the

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:58.413
board is governed, with utilities first, overlapping work removed, and any needed changes

00:02:58.413 --> 00:02:59.293
to provincial law.

00:02:59.693 --> 00:03:03.953
Another asks how to fund costly infrastructure without bills households cannot carry.

00:03:04.533 --> 00:03:09.493
Fairer contributions from each level of government, tighter financial controls, an outside look

00:03:09.493 --> 00:03:12.773
at major capital projects, and steadier long-term financing.

00:03:13.433 --> 00:03:17.633
Buchanan has long criticized higher North Shore utility bills from overruns at the North

00:03:17.633 --> 00:03:21.773
Shore Waste Water Treatment Plant, and she has called for an independent public inquiry

00:03:21.773 --> 00:03:23.653
and a fairer split of that cost.

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:25.813
A third piece would open decisions up,

00:03:25.953 --> 00:03:28.113
so directors have what they need to oversee the place

00:03:28.113 --> 00:03:28.953
and face residents.

00:03:29.493 --> 00:03:32.253
She says real reform will take longer than 100 days,

00:03:32.653 --> 00:03:34.073
and the job now is a direction,

00:03:34.593 --> 00:03:35.753
fixes where they can be made,

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:37.033
and a credible roadmap.

00:03:37.613 --> 00:03:39.953
The window lines up with the government's first legislative

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:42.553
sitting, expected in spring 2027,

00:03:42.933 --> 00:03:45.513
